RANLIB(1)                   User Commands                   RANLIB(1)

NAME
    ranlib - write the symbol index of archives

SYNOPSIS
    ranlib [-DUt] archive...

DESCRIPTION
    ranlib writes the symbol index of each archive. The index lists the
    defined global symbols of the ELF members in the order of the members
    and of their symbol tables. The linker reads the index to select
    the members that satisfy undefined symbols. nm -s prints the index. The command ar s
    writes the same index.

    ranlib rewrites the archive through a temporary file. The dates and
    owners of the members are unchanged. An archive without ELF members
    receives no index.

OPTIONS
    -D  Write the date 0 into the index member.
    -U  Write the current time into the index member. This is the
        default.
    -t  Rewrite nothing. When the archive has an index that is older
        than the archive, set the date of the index to the modification
        time of the archive plus 60 seconds. An archive without an
        index gives the message "no archive map to update".
    -h, --help
        Print the usage and exit.
    -v, --version
        Print the version and exit.

EXAMPLES
    ranlib libm.a
    ranlib -D libm.a

SEE ALSO
    ar(1), nm(1), ld(1)
